# pixi environments
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml

# pixi build/publish output -- `pixi build` writes the built package
# directly into the current directory by default
*.conda

# generated test artifacts
tests/_test_*.bmp
tests/_test_*.png

# modo doc-generator binary (scripts/install-modo.sh) and its
# `mojo doc` JSON input -- regenerated by `pixi run docs`, not
# committed.
.tools/
docs/src/*.json

# docs/src/examples/ is entirely generated -- the .md pages by
# scripts/gen_example_docs.mojo, the standalone .mojo programs extract_
# docstring_examples.mojo extracts (one per `Example:` docstring
# section, then compiled/run for real by scripts/run_parallel.sh -- see
# pixi.toml's own `example` task), and the .svg/.png/.bmp images those
# programs' own save() calls write -- all sourced from dataviz_mojo/
# *.mojo's own `Example:` docstring sections, one generated-docs-
# content location rather than a second, separately-gitignored build
# directory for the .mojo files alone. Only docs/src/_index.md, the
# landing page, is real hand-written source. Modo's own generated Hugo
# content and Hugo's own built static site are generated too, from
# docs/src/ -- none of this is committed; all of it is deployed
# straight to GitHub Pages by .github/workflows/docs.yml's own
# Actions-based deploy, regenerated fresh on every run. docs/site/'s
# own Hugo *project* files (hugo.yaml, go.mod/go.sum) ARE committed --
# those are real source, not output.
# EXCEPTION: docs/src/examples/quickstart/*.mojo -- real, hand-written
# source behind docs/src/quickstart.md's own step-by-step tutorial
# (see pixi.toml's own `example-quickstart` task and its comment next
# to `example` above), not extracted from a docstring like everything
# else in this directory, so there's nothing else that would recreate
# them if they weren't committed. Their own out_*.svg output stays
# gitignored though, same as every other rendered image in this repo
# -- `example-quickstart` regenerates those, it just needs the .mojo
# files themselves to still be there after a fresh checkout to run.
# Git can't re-include a file whose parent directory is itself
# excluded (a single blanket `docs/src/examples/` -- see `man
# gitignore`'s own "It is not possible to re-include a file if a
# parent directory of that file is excluded" note), so this walks down
# one level at a time instead, un-excluding exactly the path needed at
# each step before re-excluding what's still generated within it.
docs/src/examples/*
!docs/src/examples/quickstart
docs/src/examples/quickstart/*
!docs/src/examples/quickstart/*.mojo
docs/site/content/
docs/site/public/
docs/site/*.lock
